HackTheBox Sherlock: Dream Job-2 Writeup
Date: March 2026  

Objective
This writeup documents the complete forensic investigation performed on HackTheBox Sherlock Dream Job-2, a scenario simulating the real-world Lazarus Group (G0032) campaign known as Operation Dream Job.
The focus was on static analysis of weaponized Office documents used as initial access vectors to deliver DRATzarus (S0694) RAT.  
All activities were conducted exclusively in Kali Linux using command-line tools to demonstrate DFIR skills, OOXML forensics, VBA macro analysis, and MITRE ATT&CK mapping.

Campaign Context & MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
Threat Actor: Lazarus Group (G0032) – North Korean state-sponsored APT.  
Campaign: Operation Dream Job (2020–ongoing) – spear-phishing via fake job offers targeting defense/aerospace sectors.  
Key Malware: DRATzarus (S0694) – advanced RAT used for persistence and C2.  

Relevant Techniques:  

  - T1566.001 (Phishing: Spearphishing Attachment)  

  - T1204.002 (User Execution: Malicious File)  

  - T1137 (Office Application Startup)  

  - T1547 (Boot or Logon Autostart Execution)  

(Full ATT&CK references maintained throughout the analysis.)

